    "title": "Game Boy Advance",
    "description": "A 3D scene featuring the Game Boy Advance in a colorful room. You can choose game play footage from one of ten games and can control the camera speed and position. You can also customize the color of the GBA and choose between the classic model, SP model, and Micro model along with a Nintendo Switch option. The music and game box will change to match the game shown. \n\nThe clock can also be customized with different colors and decorations.\n\nThe Classic GBA model was done by Spicy_Apples.\nThe models of the Game Boy Advance SP and its cartridge were created by thegraphicsgeek.\nThe clock model was created by igor-tkachenko.\nThe Mini-Mario model was created by Twilighter.\nThe model used for the room (Ribbon Road) was ripped from Mario Kart 8 by Ray Koopa.\nThe e-Reader model was ripped by Centrixe the Dodo.\nThe Bulbasaur doll model was ripped from Pokémon Channel by lemurboy12.\nThe Nintendo Switch model was ripped from Super Mario Party by DogToon64.\nThe Joy-Con models were ripped from Game Builder Garage by DogToon64.\nThe Free Cam was coded by Gariam.\nI recorded the footage myself. (Hopefully I didn't play too badly!)\n\nResource Rippers:\nchristopherparaujo1989 | Frario | Xando | JonathanEx | Lexou | Grim | A.J. Nitro | neoglitch17 | Starlequin | jdaster64 | BlueYoshi-57EML | Random Talking Bush | Ryan914 | Solink | Smalls | MishuK9 | LF | Tsuka | TJ the Kid | cl.exe | Linkin800 | Mr. C | Mario Gamer | YoshiCLONE | Desgardes | Depressed Mario | Brewster T. Koopa\n\nSource Games:\nSuper Mario Advance 2: Super Mario World | Super Mario Advance 3: Yoshi's Island | WarioWare, Inc.: Mega Microgame$! | The Legend of Zelda: The Minish Cap | Metroid: Zero Mission | Kirby & the Amazing Mirror | Pokémon Emerald Version | Banjo-Kazooie: Grunty's Revenge | Sonic Advance | Rayman 3 | Mario Kart 8 | Splatoon 2 | Game & Watch Gallery 4 | Mario & Luigi: Superstar Saga | Mario Kart: Super Circuit | Wario Land 4 | DK: King of Swing | Kirby: Nightmare in Dream Land | Mother 3 | Pokémon FireRed and LeafGreen Versions | Fire Emblem: The Blazing Blade | Dragon Quest Monsters: Caravan Heart | Pikmin 4 | Pokémon Channel\n\nAdditionally, various e-Reader card scans were used related to the following games:\nSuper Mario Advance 4: Super Mario Bros. 3 | Mario Party-e | Pikmin 2 | Pokémon Trading Card Game | Baseball | Animal Crossing | Mario Bros.",
